# REJECTED -- raise the custom all-reduce one-shot/two-shot crossover to 1 MiB
#
# Base       /sgl-workspace/aiter @ d9e5ef7ce08ee7045d583aed768cff41aa9210fe
#            (aiter is vendored as a git checkout inside the container image
#             harbor.crusoe.primus-safe.amd.com/hyperloom-image/sglang:v0.5.17-rocm720-mi35x-profilerfix)
#
# Apply      cd /sgl-workspace/aiter
#            git apply /path/to/rejected/allreduce_1stage_crossover_1mib.patch
#            python3 -c "from aiter.jit.core import build_module; build_module('module_custom_all_reduce')"
#            # restart the server -- the decode path is HIP-graph captured
#
# Revert     git checkout csrc/include/custom_all_reduce.cuh   (and rebuild, or restore the stock .so)
#
# Hypothesis The TP=4 decode all-reduce moves 64 x 4096 x 2 B = 512 KiB and the profile times it at
#            10.73 us, i.e. ~71 GB/s -- an order of magnitude under the fabric, so it looked
#            latency-bound rather than bandwidth-bound. Two-shot (reduce-scatter + all-gather) halves
#            the bytes on the wire but pays a second device-wide barrier. At 512 KiB with only 4 ranks
#            the barrier should dominate, so one-shot should win. aiter's threshold for world_size <= 4
#            is 160 KiB; the legacy vllm path a hundred lines further down the same file uses 512 KiB,
#            which is what suggested the threshold was inherited rather than measured on gfx950.
#
# Measured   ISL 8192 / OSL 1024 / concurrency 64 / 192 prompts / TP=4. Four runs, first discarded
#            as cold per protocol. results/ar_1stage_512k/.
#
#              run                                tok/s   TTFT ms   TPOT ms   ITL ms
#              20260820_123524 (cold, discarded)  2386.011  5035.3    21.92    17.34
#              20260820_123703                    2412.552  5032.3    21.62    17.28
#              20260820_123840                    2410.467  5048.6    21.63    17.28
#              20260820_124018                    2411.991  5027.5    21.63    17.29
#
#            Warm mean 2411.67 vs a 2505.50 baseline = -3.75%, ~6x the 0.65% noise floor.
#            Mean TPOT 20.64 -> 21.63 ms and median ITL 16.25 -> 17.28 ms; TTFT unchanged, exactly the
#            signature of a change that only touches decode-sized messages. No gsm8k run: a regression
#            does not need a correctness gate.
#
# Verdict    Refuted, and informatively so. On this node one-shot is *worse* than two-shot at 512 KiB,
#            so the collective at decode is not barrier-bound -- AMD's 160 KiB crossover is well chosen
#            and the 512 KiB legacy vllm constant is the stale one. Combined with the fabric measurement
#            in FINDINGS.md section 5 (60.5 GB/s per directed xGMI link, RCCL already at 94% of it,
#            quickreduce-Q8 at 1.47x RCCL) this closes the collective as a source of headroom on this
#            configuration.
#
# See        FINDINGS.md, "What was tried" attempt #2.
#
diff --git a/csrc/include/custom_all_reduce.cuh b/csrc/include/custom_all_reduce.cuh
index ee304c1..7152a6f 100644
--- a/csrc/include/custom_all_reduce.cuh
+++ b/csrc/include/custom_all_reduce.cuh
@@ -3768,7 +3768,7 @@ class CustomAllreduce
         }
         else if(full_nvlink_)
         {
-            if((world_size_ <= 4 && bytes < 160 * 1024) || (world_size_ <= 8 && bytes < 80 * 1024))
+            if((world_size_ <= 4 && bytes <= 1024 * 1024) || (world_size_ <= 8 && bytes < 80 * 1024))
             {
                 call_1stage = true;
             }
